"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT2c, negative surgical margins, and no invasion of the seminal vesicles. The biopsy revealed Gleason 3+4 with tertiary pattern 4, and a subsequent biopsy showed Gleason 3+3. No lymph nodes were removed, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. Preoperative PSA was 5.2.\n\nThe prognosis is influenced by the favorable surgical findings, including negative margins and absence of seminal vesicle invasion. However, the absence of nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The preoperative PSA level is a factor, though its subsequent trajectory is unknown due to missing postoperative PSA data. The discrepancy between biopsy and prostatectomy findings is noted. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would significantly revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 74.28 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 44.57–103.99 months; its coverage has not been validated."
